","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that reports each edge once, by its position, from the end that reaches it first. The tree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"edge into a vertex is not reported again from it, so a parallel edge to the parent is a back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. It holds a copy of the graph and can be iterated more than once, and keeps its own stack."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/UndirectedEdgeDepthFirstSearch"}}}